From cd89ffaf777903ce29b69f633a64c3d8c1d9b6af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiping Ma <yipingma@berkeley.edu>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:38:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [chore] adapt to non-negative bound goal of pHL rnd
 (EasyCrypt#1135)

EasyCrypt#1135 makes the pHL `rnd` tactic (upper-bound form) emit an extra
last goal `forall &hr, 0%r <= bd`, closed automatically only when trivial.
The symbolic bounds here (`mu1 sampleto witness` and its `c%r *` multiples
in SecureORO/SecureRO, `(2*max_size)%r / (2^c)%r` in Gcol/Gext) are not,
so each `rnd` now discharges that goal explicitly (`smt(ge0_mu1 mu_bounded)`
resp. `apply eps_ge0`) before the script continues on the program-logic goal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
